// D15084 — a list typed by a single numeric literal, `1[]`, delivered to every position. It
// rides its base scalar's list as `(1 | 2)[]` does; the proof reads an element and the length.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/README.md, "Template format".
// @@PRELUDE@@
function mk(): 1[] { return [1, 1] }
// @@VALUE@@
mk()
// @@TYPE@@
1[]
// @@PROOF@@
print(v[1] + v.length)
// @@WANT@@
3
// @@VALUE2@@
[1]
// @@TYPE2@@
1[]
// @@PROOF2@@
print(v.length)
// @@WANT2@@
1
// @@SKIP@@
is_in_if: the value is a plain list, not a union — there is no arm to test it against
is_in_while: same
is_in_and: same
is_in_not: same
else_if: same
early_return_guard: same
